From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 20:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: dw9807-vcm: don't disable the regulator twice on system
 suspend

The same pair of callbacks is used for runtime PM and for system sleep:

	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(dw9807_vcm_suspend, dw9807_vcm_resume)
	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(dw9807_vcm_suspend, dw9807_vcm_resume, NULL)

The VCM is idle almost all of the time, so runtime PM has normally already
suspended it -- and disabled its regulator -- by the time the system
suspends. The system sleep callback then runs regardless and calls
regulator_disable() a second time, which fails with -EIO on the unbalanced
disable. That error is returned to the PM core:

  dw9807 12-000c: PM: dpm_run_callback(): dw9807_vcm_suspend returns -5
  dw9807 12-000c: PM: failed to suspend async: error -5
  PM: Some devices failed to suspend, or early wake event detected

and it aborts the whole suspend, so a phone with the camera driver loaded
never suspends at all. Measured on a Xiaomi POCO X3 NFC (sm7150): every
suspend attempt returned after ~2 s instead of sleeping.

Note the driver already knows about this hazard -- remove() guards the very
same regulator_disable() with pm_runtime_status_suspended() -- it just was
never applied to the system sleep path.

Use pm_runtime_force_suspend()/pm_runtime_force_resume(), which skip the
callback when the device is already runtime suspended and restore the
runtime PM state on resume. Nothing else is needed: the driver already calls
pm_runtime_set_active() + pm_runtime_enable() in probe().

Signed-off-by: Eduardo García-Mádico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9807-vcm.c b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9807-vcm.c
index 7d1df1af3..d8d7b1ac4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9807-vcm.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9807-vcm.c
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id dw9807_of_table[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, dw9807_of_table);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops dw9807_pm_ops = {
-	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(dw9807_vcm_suspend, dw9807_vcm_resume)
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(dw9807_vcm_suspend, dw9807_vcm_resume, NULL)
 };
 
